; SiO2. silicon dioxide. the most abundant compound in earth's crust.
; crystalline form: quartz — hard (7 Mohs), piezoelectric, transparent.
; amorphous form: glass — no crystal lattice, isotropic, transparent.
; window glass: SiO2 + Na2O + CaO (soda-lime glass)
; borosilicate: SiO2 + B2O3 — heat resistant (Pyrex)
; sand is predominantly SiO2. concrete = SiO2 + CaO + H2O (silicate hydrate).
; silica gel: amorphous SiO2 with high surface area — desiccant.
; semiconductor: SiO2 is the gate oxide in MOSFET transistors.

